    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths feels like a bridge between abstract ideas and real-world problem-solving—something I can’t ignore but also find fascinating when broken down into patterns. It’s not intimidating; it’s more like a puzzle where the pieces reveal meaning. My extraversion (high score) makes collaborative math projects fun, while my neuroticism sometimes makes me double-check steps to avoid mistakes.",
